title: 'fungible: allow deposits below ED into accounts with funds on hold'
doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |
      `pallet-balances`' `can_deposit` and `increase_balance` treated any account whose free
      balance would stay below the existential deposit as a new account, even when it had funds
      on hold or frozen. pallet-balances keeps such accounts alive via their provider reference,
      so this was wrong for them. A `BestEffort` deposit returned `Ok(0)` and credited nothing,
      which is how small staking rewards were lost, and `Exact` deposits and transfers failed with
      `BelowMinimum`. Nomination pool members who staked their whole balance could not claim a
      reward below ED, or unbond, since unbond claims pending rewards first.

      pallet-balances now only treats an account as new when it has no provider reference,
      matching `try_mutate_account`'s own dust decision, which no longer dusts an account with a
      provider regardless of free balance. New accounts still cannot be created below ED.

      This also fixes releasing a hold back into an account whose free balance is already below
      ED: `release` used to drop the hold first, which dusted the account since nothing was left
      to keep it alive, then tried to credit the released funds into what `try_mutate_account` had
      already reset, silently discarding them. The account's provider reference now keeps it alive
      through both steps.
crates:
  - name: frame-support
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-balances
    bump: minor
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: none
